-   entry .proportionalMixing   the layer replaces the backdrop: a weighted average by parts; any model
-   entry .multiplyMixing   `backdrop × layer`: always darker, as inks or filters combine
-   entry .screenMixing   `1 - (1 - backdrop)(1 - layer)`: always lighter, as projected lights combine
-   entry .darkenMixing   the lesser coordinate of the two
-   entry .lightenMixing   the greater coordinate of the two
-   entry .differenceMixing   the absolute difference of the two
-   entry .exclusionMixing   `backdrop + layer - 2·backdrop·layer`: like difference, with less contrast
-   entry .linearDodgeMixing   the sum, capped at `1`
-   entry .linearBurnMixing   the sum less `1`, floored at `0`
-   entry .hardLightMixing   multiply where the layer is dark, screen where it is light
-   entry .overlayMixing   multiply where the backdrop is dark, screen where it is light: hard light with the operands exchanged
-   entry .softLightMixing   a gentler hard light, by the W3C formula
-   entry .colorDodgeMixing   the backdrop brightened by the layer: `backdrop / (1 - layer)`, capped at `1`
-   entry .colorBurnMixing   the backdrop darkened by the layer: `1 - (1 - backdrop) / layer`, floored at `0`
+   entry .proportionalMixing   la capa sustituye al fondo: una media ponderada por partes; cualquier modelo
+   entry .multiplyMixing   `backdrop × layer`: siempre más oscuro, como se combinan tintas o filtros
+   entry .screenMixing   `1 - (1 - backdrop)(1 - layer)`: siempre más claro, como se combinan luces proyectadas
+   entry .darkenMixing   la menor de las dos coordenadas
+   entry .lightenMixing   la mayor de las dos coordenadas
+   entry .differenceMixing   la diferencia absoluta de las dos
+   entry .exclusionMixing   `backdrop + layer - 2·backdrop·layer`: como la diferencia, con menos contraste
+   entry .linearDodgeMixing   la suma, limitada a `1`
+   entry .linearBurnMixing   la suma menos `1`, con un mínimo de `0`
+   entry .hardLightMixing   multiplicación donde la capa es oscura, trama donde es clara
+   entry .overlayMixing   multiplicación donde el fondo es oscuro, trama donde es claro: luz fuerte con los operandos intercambiados
+   entry .softLightMixing   una luz fuerte más suave, según la fórmula del W3C
+   entry .colorDodgeMixing   el fondo aclarado por la capa: `backdrop / (1 - layer)`, limitado a `1`
+   entry .colorBurnMixing   el fondo oscurecido por la capa: `1 - (1 - backdrop) / layer`, con un mínimo de `0`

